A||||5||henrik||connection from FRONT valve train cover||||1||
Z||000000||henrik||07-19-2000||04:15 PM||||I've just done a V6 engine swap on my -85 2m4 SE. My problem is that I don't know where the hose from the FRONT valve train cover should go. The new engine is from a -87 GT. Anyone got a picture of what it should look like?||||reg||1
Z||000001||StuGood||07-19-2000||05:17 PM||||Are you talking about the PCV hose that comes out of the valve cover?||||reg||5
Z||000002||StuGood||07-20-2000||12:20 AM||||...If that's what we're talking about, then the PCV pipe goes from valve cover to the big, flexible intake duct (left of throttle body).<P>I'm surprised more members didn't chime in on this  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"><P>||||reg||12
Z||000003||henrik||07-20-2000||05:16 AM||||OK thanks! I've got another one for you. On the right hand side of the engine (just above the belts)there is a black plastic "thing" with electric connections.(EGR vacuum solenoid??) It has a small pipe in the front pointing forward. I guess that there should be a hose connected but where should it go?<BR>  / Henrik||||reg||1
Z||000004||StuGood||07-20-2000||01:05 PM||||I've answered this one before.  You are correct, the black cylindrical thing on RHS (right hand side - passenger side of car) is the EGR solenoid.  The hose on the forward end - attaches to a metal line on the forward firewall, which eventually goes to the "clean" side of the air cleaner.  ||||reg||6
Z||000005||henrik||07-28-2000||08:09 AM||||OK thanks! I'll probably get a longer hose that reaches the air cleaner directly.<BR>Thank you again for your time!   ||||reg||6
